WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:08.491
They spent fifty years trying to make it look as though I was only ever here by

2
00:00:08.491 --> 00:00:10.749
their leave. I never gave it to them.

3
00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:18.605
Just sign here, Mr Williams. A monthly tenancy. Eight shillings. A formality.

4
00:00:19.055 --> 00:00:23.104
A tenancy? On ground my family has always worked?

5
00:00:23.554 --> 00:00:24.717
Don't sign it, Dad.

6
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:29.432
Once it's on their paper, they'll say we were only ever here on their say-so.

7
00:00:29.882 --> 00:00:31.174
He was seventy-two.

8
00:00:31.174 --> 00:00:35.935
They coaxed him into a tenancy, to make our occupancy look permissive.

9
00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.771
That was their first paper.

10
00:00:40.141 --> 00:00:43.694
Western Ground Rents would like you to take up a fresh agreement.

11
00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:48.663
No. My father's agreement died with him. I'll sign nothing.

12
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:55.395
In June nineteen fifty, Mr Knapp, an estate agent from Penarth,

13
00:00:55.395 --> 00:00:59.549
brought a lodger to stay with us. He stayed about two years.

14
00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:02.546
Later the lodger came back, and told me.

15
00:01:02.546 --> 00:01:07.705
Mr Knapp had asked him to look for the papers my father had relating to the farm.

16
00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:12.979
He had taken the papers from the blanket box, the agreement relating to the farm,

17
00:01:12.979 --> 00:01:14.585
and given them to Mr Knapp.

18
00:01:15.039 --> 00:01:18.435
I looked in the blanket box. The papers were gone.

19
00:01:18.885 --> 00:01:23.874
Thirty-seven years later, the court would say our papers were never produced.

20
00:01:26.245 --> 00:01:29.024
I came home from the hospital with one leg.

21
00:01:29.024 --> 00:01:32.514
They were already on my land, both sides of the house.

22
00:01:32.965 --> 00:01:35.081
We have a possession order, madam.

23
00:01:35.531 --> 00:01:41.644
Not for this house you haven't. This is my home, and I own it. Now get off my land.

24
00:01:44.014 --> 00:01:48.612
A proper tenancy. A fair rent. It would settle everything.

25
00:01:49.062 --> 00:01:51.753
It would settle it your way. No.

26
00:01:54.142 --> 00:01:58.113
One more offer. Sign, and you'll never be troubled again.

27
00:01:58.582 --> 00:02:01.978
Same answer as nineteen thirty-nine. No.

28
00:02:04.348 --> 00:02:10.226
Then the same men came back in different coats. Western Ground Rents became BP.

29
00:02:12.628 --> 00:02:17.226
In nineteen sixty-nine BP bought the seized land all around me.

30
00:02:17.676 --> 00:02:22.435
And they bought the interest, not the title, in an order against my home.

31
00:02:22.435 --> 00:02:25.304
An order that was never legally enforceable.

32
00:02:27.356 --> 00:02:32.424
My Lord, she holds no title. We ask the court to extinguish her claim.

33
00:02:32.876 --> 00:02:36.350
I will not do that. This matter is adjourned.

34
00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.371
We hold an order from nineteen sixty-two. You are to leave.

35
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.973
That order was never enforceable.

36
00:02:44.973 --> 00:02:49.434
It rests on the nineteen fifty-five order, and that was for Parcel B.

37
00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:51.826
A different piece of land altogether.

38
00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.918
What is this place to you?

39
00:02:56.368 --> 00:03:00.966
It's my home. It always has been. And I'm not going anywhere.

40
00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:07.450
My client's position is clear. This is her home, and she is staying in it.

41
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:15.142
Then, quietly, out of my sight, BP and my own lawyer shook hands.

42
00:03:17.192 --> 00:03:20.722
It's good news. BP have offered to let you stay.

43
00:03:20.722 --> 00:03:26.900
The nineteen sixty-two order is quashed. You're there on licence now, and BP own it.

44
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.548
There's nothing more you need to do.

45
00:03:31.598 --> 00:03:36.415
Dear Sirs. The nineteen fifty-five order was for Parcel B, not my home.

46
00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:41.707
Western Ground Rents should never have taken the land either side of my house.

47
00:03:42.158 --> 00:03:44.152
I know what this is. A racket.

48
00:03:44.152 --> 00:03:49.269
They draw up one-sided papers to make it look as if I'm here on their say-so.

49
00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:52.924
Twelve years later they take them to the Land Registry,

50
00:03:52.924 --> 00:03:54.984
and register my land as theirs.

51
00:03:55.438 --> 00:03:59.652
The council did it on one side of my house in nineteen seventy.

52
00:03:59.652 --> 00:04:05.205
Cardiff Corporation on the other, in sixty-one, sixty-two. Both after twelve years.

53
00:04:05.205 --> 00:04:10.824
And Parcel B in fifty-two, twelve years after that dubious agreement in thirty-nine.

54
00:04:11.278 --> 00:04:17.165
Now BP, twelve years after their order, dress it up as stopping the clock on me,

55
00:04:17.165 --> 00:04:21.727
on land I own. That is beyond white collar crime. It is fraud.

56
00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:28.459
In nineteen eighty-three BP registered my land in their names.

57
00:04:28.909 --> 00:04:33.045
They didn't tell the Land Registry I was asserting ownership.

58
00:04:33.045 --> 00:04:38.470
And they didn't tell me. I died weeks later. Only then did my family hear of it.

59
00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.811
BP are entitled to take possession of the whole farm.

60
00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:50.113
In nineteen eighty-seven the court gave BP possession of the whole farm.

61
00:04:52.483 --> 00:04:55.247
While my son William was still appealing,

62
00:04:55.247 --> 00:05:00.842
BP and the Land Registry merged the titles. Then they called it all the whole farm.

63
00:05:03.212 --> 00:05:06.608
Their Lordships decline William Buckler's application.

64
00:05:08.978 --> 00:05:13.262
This farm is BP's property. Everybody out. Now.

65
00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:16.335
Then they came for my son's family.

66
00:05:16.335 --> 00:05:20.533
Fifteen police and five BP bailiffs, all around Branwen.

67
00:05:20.533 --> 00:05:25.180
She was pregnant, with three little ones. Two boys and a girl.

68
00:05:25.632 --> 00:05:31.588
Twenty men, for one woman and three babies. Same men. Different coats.

69
00:05:31.888 --> 00:05:34.251
Mrs Buckler says she was assaulted and her shoulder

70
00:05:34.251 --> 00:05:35.807
dislocated when she came to serve

71
00:05:35.807 --> 00:05:39.345
that injunction today, but she remains optimistic about

72
00:05:39.345 --> 00:05:40.567
regaining her home.

73
00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:44.614
We won a small victory today in getting the injunction and

74
00:05:44.614 --> 00:05:45.250
stopping them from doing any

75
00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:47.982
further damage to our home.

76
00:05:47.982 --> 00:05:51.127
And all we have to do now is hope that the judge will uphold

77
00:05:51.127 --> 00:05:53.568
this decision on Friday when there's a full hearing.

78
00:05:55.638 --> 00:05:57.989
Then they bulldozed the house.

79
00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:03.206
The application is declared inadmissible.

80
00:06:03.656 --> 00:06:08.567
William took it to the European Court of Human Rights. He lost there too.

81
00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:13.550
They're building houses on my mother's farm.

82
00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.926
I'll petition against every one of them.

83
00:06:16.377 --> 00:06:22.032
He died petitioning against the houses they built on our farm. He never gave it up.

84
00:06:22.032 --> 00:06:22.986
Neither did I.

